<title>UK: Aquarius shares set debut premium.</title>
<headline>Aquarius shares set debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Aquarius Group Plc set a premium on their first day of trading on London Stock Exchange on Friday.</p>
<p>By 1335 GMT the shares were quoted at 172-1/2p, 6-1/2p ahead of their 166p issue price. Volume reached 329,800 shares.</p>
<p>Aquarius designs and makes lampshades, bathroom accessories and acrylic baths. It is the fourth group to be floated by Gartland Whalley and Barker Plc, a corporate developer.</p>
<p>The float, which raised a net 8.8 million stg, valued Aquarius at 34.2 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7945</p>
